     3	# Name: 背景色编码周期加虚线轨迹
     4	#
     5	# Design analysis for the combo:
     6	# - Concrete behavior: the original task paints every beam step as teal. Here the
     7	#   beam geometry is unchanged, but the main-grid background color becomes a
     8	#   global dash parameter. If bg=3, each beam paints 3 translated square-steps,
     9	#   leaves 1 translated square-step as background, then repeats. Turns still come
    10	#   only from the legend. Example: a north-going beam with steps s1..s8 was
    11	#   solid in the base task; now with bg=3 it paints s1,s2,s3, skips s4, paints
    12	#   s5,s6,s7, skips s8. If it turns after s5, the count continues across the
    13	#   corner so the dashed trail follows the whole path rather than each segment
    14	#   resetting independently.
    15	# - Complexity calibration: only the paint schedule changes; obstacle geometry,
    16	#   square width, and legend parsing stay stable. To keep the variation visible
    17	#   and learnable, the generator uses only bg in {2,3,4} and cycles them across
    18	#   calls, so train/test sets are likely to show repeated support instead of a
    19	#   one-off arbitrary color-id mapping.
    20	# - Assumption audit against the original main():
    21	#   1. "Every empty move paints teal" is no longer valid; painting must depend on
    22	#      a step counter and the bg-derived period.
    23	#   2. Obstacle detection must not depend on already-painted trail cells, because
    24	#      skipped dash cells remain bg; the solver therefore reads obstacle colors
    25	#      from the immutable cropped base grid.
    26	#   3. The original output could match the solid-path baseline when all paths are
    27	#      short. The generator now rejects such cases by comparing dashed and solid
    28	#      outputs and requiring visible missing teal cells.
    29	# - Placement legality: the generator keeps the original edge-touching rectangle
    30	#   construction and path-first span constraints, so obstacles remain disjoint,
    31	#   in-bounds, and at least one cell away from the teal square.
    32	# - Visual observability / neatness: only one extra visual layer is added, namely
    33	#   regular one-step gaps inside the existing teal tracks. The generator requires
    34	#   multiple skipped dash steps and a measurable teal-count drop versus the solid
    35	#   baseline so the combo is plainly visible instead of degenerating back to the
    36	#   original task.
